# Multiplayer

## Authority
- **Host**: combat/morph terrain authority per the existing session model; animal herds + `world` snapshot.
- **Client**: applies `pose`, `cast`, `knock`, `beast`, `world`; does not run host-only herd simulation.

## Intents (`net/intents.js`)
| kind | Note |
|------|------|
| `pose` | movement source of truth ~`CONFIG.netPoseInterval` |
| `walk` | **no-op** (compat) — do not put movement back here |
| `cast` | `spells.castAs` locally on every client |
| `knock` | low-latency; dedupe via `seq` vs pose.knock |
| `beast` / `world` | host → clients; host ignores inbound |

## Checklist when changing sync
- [ ] No unnecessary full state every frame (intervals from CONFIG).
- [ ] Remote wizard: `w.remote === true`, interpolation `netPoseInterpDelay`.
- [ ] Tab hide: `pageCatchUpMax` / `pageCatchUpStep` — do not let dt explode.
- [ ] Same map seed / spawn logic on all clients.

## Anti-patterns
- Simulating critters on non-host without `markHerdRemote`.
- Damaging a remote wizard “locally” outside the agreed cast/knock flow.
- New intent without a handler in `createGameIntentHandlers`.
